Codec 2 1.2.0 for MSVC, whose C compiler has no variable-length arrays.

Each VLA in the vocoder files becomes _alloca of the same size, on the same
line, except levinson_durbin's two-dimensional one, which becomes a fixed
array bounded by lpc.h's LPC_MAX_ORDER, with an assert. No behaviour changes.
Written by Revenant against libcodec2's own source, generated mechanically at
each site MSVC rejected; it is libcodec2's expression, modified, and stays
under libcodec2's LGPL-2.1.

